[2026-09-20 12:19:23 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 001]   TEP-9 step 001 -- JPL SBDB download
[2026-09-20 12:19:23 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 001]   Downloads the JPL Small-Body Database (SBDB) orbital-element catalog
[2026-09-20 12:19:23 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 001]   for the outer solar system via the public sbdb_query API
[2026-09-20 12:19:23 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 001]   (https://ssd-api.jpl.nasa.gov/doc/sbdb_query.html).
[2026-09-20 12:19:23 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 001]   Three real-data samples are fetched:
[2026-09-20 12:19:23 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 001]   1. Outer solar system asteroids: all bodies with heliocentric
[2026-09-20 12:19:23 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 001]   semimajor axis a >= 30 AU (classical Kuiper belt, resonant,
[2026-09-20 12:19:23 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 001]   scattered, detached and extreme trans-Neptunian objects).
[2026-09-20 12:19:23 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 001]   2. Centaurs (orbit class CEN): the Neptune-crossing population,
[2026-09-20 12:19:23 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 001]   used for the cross-population coherence test.
[2026-09-20 12:19:23 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 001]   3. Comets reaching the outer system (q >= 5 AU): the Jupiter-family
[2026-09-20 12:19:23 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 001]   and Halley-type population used for anti-axis directionality.
[2026-09-20 12:19:23 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 001]   Outputs
